'' A 'const as ustring' IN A CONCATENATION WITH A RUNTIME TERM, PRINTED. 'print n & G' was
'' a ustring chain -- ConcatTermsAreU_ asks G's type -- in which StrTermFlavour_ called G
'' NEUTRAL, like a literal, so LowerUStrChain found no UTF-16 term, declined, and the
'' statement was dropped: TKO0994, the book's ch03/declare.tiko. The constant is now a
'' UTF-16 term (src/mir/lowerterm.bas). fbc-modern 1.20 has no 'const as ustring' (error
'' 24), so there is no differential; the expected text is the concatenation itself.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/const-ustring-concat.bas -o tests/driver/constustrconcat.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/constustrconcat.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/constustrconcat.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3hi
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hi3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3 hi
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Shi|hiS
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: Uhi|xhi
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3s
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3hi|3hi| 3 3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 3hi
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
